@defgroup micro-test-plus-logical-functions Logical Functions
@brief Functions used to compose logical expressions in tests.

@details
The functions `mt::_and()`, `mt::_or()`, and `mt::_not()` combine multiple
conditions, allowing expressive and concise test logic.

These function names are prefixed with an underscore to avoid clashes with
language alternative tokens or related macros named `and`, `or`, and
`not`. Using these logical functions allows developers to express compound
conditions clearly and improve readability.

@par Example

@code{.cpp}
ts.test ("Check compound conditions", [] (auto& t) {
  t.expect (mt::_and (mt::eq (compute_answer (), 42),
                      mt::eq (compute_float (), 42.0)));
});
@endcode

When operands are function comparators, use the overloaded logical
operators `&&`, `||`, and `!` provided in the `micro_test_plus::operators`
namespace for more natural logical expressions.
